{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 — RED-first fix (proven)\n\n**Fix.** `tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py::test_resign_routes_through_pin_collecting_sign_path`\nnow stubs `gate_source.resolve_gate_handle` (returns a benign handle, records the call) and\n`gate_source.gate_read_root` (nullcontext) — the exact isolation the two sibling public-resign\ntests already apply. A `gate_handle_calls` spy asserts resign still routes signing through the\nattested gate seam, so the sandbox does not mask a routing regression.\n\n**RED-first oracle (empirical).** With `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` at an empty scratch dir:\n- RED (stubs removed = pre-fix behavior): a bounded 22s run materialized **62,984** real\n  snapshot files (climbing toward the full 124,994 / 1.1 GB) before being killed mid-write —\n  the real HEAD code tree + 121k-file tickets branch. This is the multi-minute post-PASS\n  `unlinkat`/`rmdir` deletion the ticket reports.\n- GREEN (fixed): the same single test passes in ~5.6s and materializes **0** files.\n\n**Suite.** Full `tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py` = 8 passed in 18.76s (previously the one\ntest alone was ~200s call + minutes of cleanup). `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass. Unrelated\ntest behavior preserved (only this test's isolation changed; the three sibling resign tests and\ntheir gate stubs are untouched).\n\n**Attribution.** caused_by 5128-0856-d80f-4eb6 (commit 1e7e5c9468f8) — added the attested gate\nsession to resign; the routing test was never retrofitted with the sibling gate stub."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787552634532457001,"uuid":"990411cb-4915-4e39-9425-61a83f4dc6ba"}